WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.320
- But you, you've actually,

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:04.000
you've delivered babies
on the show, so, what,

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.640
what were the births
of your own kids like?

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:06.730
Were they intense?

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:07.743
I was so ready to get mine out.

00:00:07.743 --> 00:00:10.704
I was just get out, get out, get out.

00:00:10.704 --> 00:00:12.660
- Yes, oh, yes.

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.811
Well, my son was huge.

00:00:14.811 --> 00:00:19.811
He was humongous and I feel
like the hippies lied to me,

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:22.940
because I was watching these documentaries

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:26.250
about these water births
and they were all, you know,

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:27.670
doing this, like, (groaning)

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:30.200
they were just, I was like,
wow, this I can do that.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.590
I can do that, I wanna do a water birth.

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:35.690
So I go to this hospital
where they actually

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:39.540
allow water births in the
hospital but my water breaks

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.110
at five in the morning, pop!

00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:42.730
I literally felt it break.

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:44.866
I was like, oh my water broke.

00:00:44.866 --> 00:00:48.010
Then the labor just
started coming really fast

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:50.000
and so I didn't have time to
stop, like, my husband's like

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.610
watch TV, it'll be hours,
it's your first baby,

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:55.187
we don't know, so, no, no, no.

00:00:55.187 --> 00:00:59.381
So we're driving and I'm
like in whatever transition

00:00:59.381 --> 00:01:01.800
in the car, I think.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:03.741
By the time I get to the
hospital, I'm nine centimeters

00:01:03.741 --> 00:01:08.273
and so I push for two hours
out of the birthing tub,

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:11.610
screaming bloody murder.

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:13.410
- Oh, god!
- And I was like,

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:14.340
he's stuck, he's stuck!

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:17.370
I kept waiting for somebody to
be like, oh, we have to take

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:20.270
him out of you via Cesarean,
emergency C-section!

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:23.753
And I was like, nobody's
coming and I'm still pushing.

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:26.180
And then they get the tub set up

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:27.610
and it didn't really seem

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:29.320
to make a difference, unfortunately.

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:32.082
(laughing)

00:01:32.082 --> 00:01:34.870
And I finally got him out
and he was like nine pounds.

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:37.700
And so, oh yeah, he was big baby.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:42.070
Big, big, big baby and
so when I got pregnant

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:45.282
with my daughter, I got a epidural.

00:01:45.282 --> 00:01:47.184
- Oh amen.

00:01:47.184 --> 00:01:48.680
(laughing and applause)

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:49.890
- I did, I did.
- Oh!

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:52.417
- And it was a beautiful
experience with like magical,

00:01:52.417 --> 00:01:55.153
because I, I should've
listened to my two friends.

00:01:55.153 --> 00:01:57.390
Two of my best friends had babies

00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:59.970
and they were like, girl, get
the epidural, don't be stupid.

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:02.870
If you're gonna take Tylenol
or Motrin for a headache

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:05.004
you're gonna need the good drugs.

00:02:05.004 --> 00:02:07.810
And it was a beautiful
experience with her.

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:09.260
I pushed her out in 20 minutes

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:13.140
and she was the glorious
happy baby, and...

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:14.640
- Dude, I'll tell you what.
- So, yeah.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:16.950
- It, I had friends tell me as well,

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:18.533
there were, there were
several different ideas

00:02:18.533 --> 00:02:20.530
of what, you know, should
happen for your birth.

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:25.530
And I was like, if God intended
for me to not have drugs

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:27.920
and not have help getting this out

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:30.130
then he wouldn't have had me born in 1982.

00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:34.820
- Word, word.
- Because I am gonna take,

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:36.290
what are you, what can you put in here

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:38.510
to make it less hurtful?

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:41.853
I was like, give me every,
the baby will be fine.

00:02:41.853 --> 00:02:43.461
I was like, does this make you want

00:02:43.461 --> 00:02:45.162
to just pop some children out?

00:02:45.162 --> 00:02:48.380
- No, it doesn't.
- Is it just like,

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:49.930
birth control, what just happened?

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:51.070
- Yep! Thank you!

